# One env file for the whole repo, read by contracts, solver and app alike.
# Three copies means three chances to hold a different RPC or a different address,
# and that kind of failure shows up as a wrong answer rather than as an error.
#
# Copy to .env and fill in. .env itself is never committed.
#
# There are no private keys here, and there never will be. Deploys are signed with
# cast wallet or a hardware wallet, passed to forge as --account or --ledger.
# Values that are production facts rather than secrets, such as the USDG address,
# live in docs/parameter.md and then in code constants, not here.

# Chain endpoints. Both official domains are intercepted by Indonesian ISP DNS, so
# these are the provider endpoints that answer without a workaround. Mainnet has
# been that way since the start. The testnet domain joined it on 19 September 2026,
# resolving to block.gmedia.id at 103.217.209.188, which presents a certificate for
# the wrong name and reads as a TLS error rather than as a block.
#
# Do not count on drpc for history. Its reach has changed three times, a window of
# 20 to 40 thousand blocks on 16 September 2026, latest only on 26 September, and
# full history on 29 September, when NVDA totalSupply differed at every block asked
# and its code was empty at block 1000. A fork that worked yesterday can stop today.
# Alchemy's free tier works for chain 4663, measured 27 September 2026. Put its
# url, key included, in your own .env and never in this file, which is committed.
# Enable Robinhood Chain Mainnet on the Alchemy app first, and allow a couple of
# minutes before it answers every call.
NOKTURN_RPC_MAINNET=https://robinhood.drpc.org
NOKTURN_RPC_TESTNET=https://robinhood-testnet.drpc.org

# The coordinator API. NOKTURN_API_RPC may list several urls separated by commas.
# The first is primary and the rest are tried in order when it fails. On the fork
# it is the local anvil.
#
# NOKTURN_API_PUBLIC_RPC is the url printed in every cast command a receipt
# carries, so a judge can run it. It must never hold a key. The API refuses to
# start when NOKTURN_API_RPC has a path, which is where a provider puts its key,
# and this one is unset.
NOKTURN_API_RPC=http://127.0.0.1:8545
NOKTURN_API_PUBLIC_RPC=
NOKTURN_API_RPC_BUDGET_PER_MINUTE=6000

# Where protocol fees, seized bonds and cross dust are sent.
NOKTURN_TREASURY=

# The one address that can stop the protocol taking on anything new. It cannot
# unpause, because a pause carries its own six hour deadline and lapses, and it
# cannot move or trap a single token. parameter.md section 8.1 and 8.2.
#
# Unlike the timelock roles this one is a parameter rather than an immutable, so a
# leaked key can be rotated out in the 48 hours the timelock takes.
NOKTURN_GUARDIAN=

# The timelock is the governor of every contract that has one, and governor is
# immutable, so these are decided before the first deploy and not after. Comma
# separated, no spaces. Proposers are also cancellers.
NOKTURN_TIMELOCK_PROPOSERS=
NOKTURN_TIMELOCK_EXECUTORS=
